@* The framework's own site on the Architecture page (F124): this site, built on the framework the way a customer's is. *@
<Band Id="site" Kicker="src/site · the framework's own site">
    <h3>This site, built on the framework.</h3>
    <p class="lede">The framework's own website is a site like any customer's: a visitor area on the framework's web, with the guide in its corner. It is the one place in <code>src/</code> that uses packs and an identity, and nothing in the framework uses it, so the engine can still leave for its own repository.</p>
    <ul class="rules">
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.site</code></strong> This site: its pages, films, graphs and styles.</li>
        <li><strong><code>louis-agent.identity.expert</code></strong> The guide in the corner: who it is, as markdown, and the docs it answers from.</li>
    </ul>
</Band>
